<title>FRANCE: Usinor has no comment on Fafer.</title>
<headline>Usinor has no comment on Fafer.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-07-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>France's Usinor declined on Friday to comment on a Belgian newspaper report that it was interested in acquiring a stake in Belgian stainless steel maker Fabrique de Fer (Fafer) if it was for sale.</p>
<p>&quot;Fafer is a bourse-listed company. We have no comment,&quot; a Usinor spokeswoman told Reuters.</p>
<p>Belgian newspaper Le Soir said Fafer's main shareholder, Belgium's Boel family, was considering selling its stake in the company because Fafer's current size meant its long-term future could not be guaranteed.</p>
<p>Le Soir said possible buyers included British steel, Belgian-Luxemburg group Arbed/Sidmar and Usinor.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5432</p>
